<title>USA: Glendale wins approval on acquisition.</title>
<headline>Glendale wins approval on acquisition.</headline>
<dateline>GLENDALE, Calif. 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Glendale Federal Bank on Wednesday said it received approval from Office of Thrift Supervision to proceed with its $63 million acquisition of TransWorld Bancorp and its principal unit, TransWorld Bank.</p>
<p>The acquisition was announced on November 4 and is set to close on May 16.</p>
<p>Glendale Federal will pay $18.25 per share for the outstanding shares of TransWorld Bancorp.</p>
<p>TransWorld Bank has 12 branches around the Los Angeles area with roughly 240 employees. Glendale Federal expects to retain most of TransWorld's employees.</p>
</text>
